{
  "requirement": "[`Sources`](../../rustdocs/trust_but_verify/sources/struct.Sources.html) supplies\nbuilt-in filesystem listing, reading, outlining, text search, and structural\nsearch. Construct it with the project directory:\n\n```rust,ignore\nuse trust_but_verify::sources::Sources;\n\nlet sources = Sources::new(repository_root);\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.sources.provider` has two obligations. `Sources` must supply built-in listing, reading, outlining, text search and structural search. It must also be constructible with `Sources::new(repository_root)`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs` shows `impl[Sources]` with `new`, `list`, `read`, `parse`, `search_text` and `search_structure`. The reviewed tests cover each of them through a real `Sources::new(root.path())`:\n\n- **Construction:** `Sources::new` is called in both integration tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs`: `gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository` and `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope`.\n- **Listing:** the gitignore test calls `sources.list` with `SourceScope::all()`, the default scope and `SourceScope::under(..)`. It asserts the exact set of listed paths, including that ignored, `.git` and `skip` files are excluded.\n- **Reading:** the gitignore test calls `read`. It asserts failure for ignored files and for `.git/config`, and success for `.gitignore`. It never asserts the content that `read` returns for a normal file. Reading the file's content is still exercised through `parse`, and in `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` through `memory.read` on a provider that returns versioned text. This is a minor weakness, not a gap, because the requirement only says reading is supplied.\n- **Outlining:** `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` calls `sources.parse`. It asserts the plain-text outline has 3 items and the fingerprint schemes are `plain-text-structural-v1` and `rust-structural-v1`. `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` also checks the outline of a parsed snapshot.\n- **Text search:** the gitignore test asserts match counts, completeness, regex patterns and scoping, and that an escaping scope (`..`) is an error. `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` asserts the exact path, line and excerpt.\n- **Structural search:** the structural test asserts the match path, selector `fn[visible]` and excerpt `call()`. It also covers limits and completeness, scoping that excludes ignored and `.git` files, language selection (Python versus Rust), and the error for an out-of-root scope.\n\nNo obligation of the subject is left untested, and no `{fixme}` is involved.",
  "references": "4d41003c77972a16520215e0fd1626c3ad65e439c7c88420a89dd4756ab62d31",
